+# Final review, cluster 15 (undo): super-auto/seat-failure-manager-seats, epic hg-k4l
+
+Source: base 0dbe4772f4cd541e6b5ecaa1dd55b9a72f62c784, head efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`; head tree 20665d254559d4c32587bd1c6020131165ca1fff). Cluster input: `src/undo/tests.rs`, slice `slices/000077.diff` (+128 lines). Source binding: `bind-review-source` exited 0.
+
+## Scope and method
+
+- Read the cluster slice, the bundle digest, the epic (`bd show hg-k4l`) and the root design doc `docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats-design.md` (Requirement baseline, §4.8, §4.9, §4.11).
+- Opened `src/undo/compensate.rs` and `src/plan/core_kinds.rs` (`write_action`, `do_retire_seat`) at head to trace the undo routes named in the spec.
+- Built and ran tests in a review-owned detached worktree at head (`.worktrees/review-c15-inv17c351e9`, target reflinked from the run worktree, `toolbox run -c ht-build` with a libz shim under the session scratchpad). The caller checkout was not touched; its HEAD stayed at efc21b6 and `git status` stayed clean throughout.
+
+## What the cluster changes
+
+- The undo test fixture `fx()` registers two test-only mutations (`reparent::testing::SetPointer`, `managers::testing::SetNodeManager`) so tests can set manager pointers and the node manager directly.
+- New tests: `guard_undo_of_creating_hydrate` (undo of the hydrate that created the node manager is refused with the `node-manager set` remedy, seat stays Active), `seat_create_has_no_undoable_action` (documents that SeatCreate writes no undoable action), `reparent_on_application_retire_records_rewrites` and `reparent_on_undo_of_hydrate` (retirement through ApplicationRetire and through undo of a hydrate reparents `r` from `lead` to `mid` and records the `{holder, field, old, new}` rewrite in the action record).
+
+## Test evidence at head
+
+- `cargo test --lib --locked --offline undo::` at head: 23 passed, 11 failed, deterministic (same 11 with `--test-threads=1`). The four new tests pass.
+- Failing: `adoption_conflict_with_active_occupant_is_repair_required`, `adoption_preview_from_bound_pane_does_not_warn_pane_closes`, `adoption_preview_with_bound_caller_pane`, `adoption_without_an_observed_pane_stays_unknown_until_the_observer_looks`, `candidates_newest_first_with_undone_marked`, `occupant_gained_between_preview_and_apply_is_rejected`, `reconnect_prevents_preboundary_retirement_undo_reactivating_old_references`, `undo_keeps_previously_dormant_seats_dormant`, `undo_plan_applied_seat_retirement_previews_and_applies_resurrection`, `undo_tab_close_cascade_restores_seat_and_clones_excluding_already_retired`, `undo_writes_compensating_action_and_marks_original_undone`.
+- Typical panic: `seat retire foreman: node manager foreman (st_...) cannot be retired; move the role first with herdr-graph plan node-manager set <seat>`; others fail with `nothing to restore` or with dormant seats unexpectedly Active.
+- Root cause: since the hg-k4l.23 merge (3456a31), `SeatCreate` makes the first seat created the node manager and forces it Active; since the hg-k4l.8 merge (eddc1e4), `make_plan` refuses to retire the node manager. The undo fixture never opts out of first-seat assignment, so the first seat each pre-existing test creates is the node manager and every test that retires or keeps it dormant breaks. The hg-k4l.23 report states "undo needed no opt-out (all passed)", but that run was on a stack without the hg-k4l.8 guard; the hg-k4l.27 report's "undo:: 32 passed" was at tree 8875fb2, which is not the head tree. Neither run reflects the composed head.
+- Probe (review worktree only, reverted afterwards): adding `crate::plan::managers::testing::opt_out(&root);` right after `init_instance(&root).unwrap();` in `fx()` makes `undo::` 34 passed, 0 failed, the four new tests included.
+- Whole `cargo test --lib` at head: 896 passed, 35 failed. Outside this cluster the same kind of failures show up in bootstrap::tests (4), observe::tests (10), plan::ops::tests (2), reconcile::tests (5) and transcripts::tests (3). That is for the seam reviewer; this cluster owns only the 11 undo failures.
+
+## Spec trace for the undo routes
+
+- §4.9 "The undo refusal for the node manager's creating action names the `node-manager set` remedy": delivered. Undo of a Hydrate delegates to the ApplicationRetire kind's `plan` (compensate.rs), so the shared `make_plan` guard refuses it; `guard_undo_of_creating_hydrate` checks the message and that the seat stays Active. Apply replans through `make_plan`, so a `node-manager set` that lands between plan and apply is also covered.
+- §4.11 / B6 "undo-driven retirement reparents through `do_retire_seat`": delivered. The undo mutate path calls ApplicationRetire's `mutate`, which goes through `do_retire_seat`/`reparent`; `write_action` stores the rewrites under `reparented`, and `finalize` relabels that record as the Undo action. Covered by `reparent_on_undo_of_hydrate`.
+- B8 through undo: the guard covers Hydrate compensation (tested). TemplateEdit compensation goes through the same `make_plan` guard but has no undo-level test.
+- §4.11 "Undo of a retirement (the `Retire` and `ApplicationRetire` action kinds) restores each pointer the reparent rewrote, but only where that pointer still holds the reparent value; others are left and listed in the undo plan": not delivered at head. `restore_preview`/`restore_mutate` never read the `reparented` compensation; the only readers of `REPARENTED_KEY` are `write_action` and the test helper `reparent::testing::recorded`. Tracked by open bead hg-k4l.17 (acceptance unchecked). Production effect: `plan retire <seat>` followed by `undo <act>` brings the seat back while its former reports stay under its manager. This is a spec-body requirement, not a Requirement baseline row (B6 asks only for reparenting on retirement, which is delivered).
+- §4.8 "undo restore goes through the shared first-seat helper": not delivered at head. Tracked by open bead hg-k4l.25 (blocked on open hg-k4l.24). B10 is satisfied through S1 ("first seat created"), and an undo restore is not a creation, so this is a spec-body gap rather than an undelivered baseline row.
+- B14 (no daemon-free fallback in `undo`'s candidate list) lives in `src/cli/undo.rs`, not in this cluster; the CLI cluster or the seam reviewer traces it.
+
+## Seam notes
+
+- The fixture break comes from two separately reviewed tasks composing (hg-k4l.23 first-seat assignment plus hg-k4l.8 retirement guard). It appears in this cluster's file, but the same pattern breaks five other test modules (counts above). The seam reviewer should treat the 35-failure `cargo test --lib` at head as one composition defect with one fix: opt-outs in every affected fixture.
+- `reparent_on_application_retire_records_rewrites` tests ApplicationRetire, not undo. It belongs with the templates/plan tests, but where it lives does not affect correctness.
+
+## Verdict
+not ready (undo test suite fails at head: 11 of 34 undo tests break because the fixture lacks the first-seat opt-out; spec 4.11 undo restore of reparented pointers is unimplemented)
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- src/undo/tests.rs fx() lacks `crate::plan::managers::testing::opt_out(&root)` after `init_instance`, so 11 of 34 `undo::` tests fail deterministically at head efc21b6 (first seat auto-becomes node manager via hg-k4l.23, then hg-k4l.8 refuses its retirement); a review-worktree probe with that one line gives 34/34 passing.
+- Spec §4.11 undo restore is unimplemented at head: undo of a Retire or ApplicationRetire action ignores the recorded `reparented` rewrites (no reader of REPARENTED_KEY in src/undo), so reparented pointers are never restored or listed; tracked by open bead hg-k4l.17, which must land before the branch does.
+- Spec §4.8 undo restore does not go through the first-seat helper at head; tracked by open bead hg-k4l.25 (blocked on open hg-k4l.24), which must land before the branch does.
+
+## Untested scope
+- Undo of a TemplateEdit whose inverse would withdraw or retire the node manager is not tested at the undo level; only Hydrate compensation is.
+- The undo plan preview for undo of a hydrate is not asserted to list the `seat.manager` reparent effect; `reparent_on_undo_of_hydrate` checks only the applied result and the action record.
+- Undo of a ClosureCascade that reparented (observed route) has no test of what happens to the recorded rewrites.
+- No undo test covers the lenient reparent fallback note (`reparent_fallback`) carried into an Undo action record.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- `reparent_on_application_retire_records_rewrites` sits in src/undo/tests.rs although it exercises ApplicationRetire, not undo; moving it is cosmetic.
+- `seat_create_has_no_undoable_action` documents a fact rather than a requirement; it costs little to keep.
